Live-reload documents when the .gkw file changes on disk

Watch each open document's file with notify; distinguish external
modifications from the app's own saves by content hash. External
changes are pushed to the renderer as a 'file-changed' event and into
Elm as FileChangedOnDisk, which re-parses and swaps the working tree.
If the document has unsaved edits (or a card is being edited), the
user is asked before reloading. This enables workflows where an agent
or editor modifies the .gkw on disk while it is open.

